"Suculpful culture that has been able to stay awake all the night still exists," he said, adding that modern technology and increasing pressure on the students meant that sleep deprivation was a growing problem.
Securing sleeping enough, and of good - quality, should be the student's secret weapon to fight stress, severe fatigue and anxiety, he said - even to avoid increasing in weight, since sleeplessness puts the mind in a hungry mode, making them hungry at all the time.
Raymond So, a student aged from California, who is studying chemistry and physical biology, has helped Professor Czeisler to design the course, after attending one of his classes last a year during his first year in Harvard.
