HIV/Aids: China reports an increase of 14% in new cases
China has announced a leap of 14% in the number of its citizens living with HIV and Aids.
More than 820,000 people are affected in the country, say health officials.
In only the second quarter of 2018 around 40,000 new cases were reported.
The vast majority of new cases have been transmitted by sex, which mark a change from the past.
Traditionally, HIV had spread quickly in some parts of China as a result of transfusions of infected blood.
But the number of people taking HIV in this way had been reduced to almost zero, said Chinese health officers at a conference in Yunnan's province.
However, year-on-adadays, the number of people living with HIV and Asdas in China has risen by 100,000 people.
